model {
  extend basalt.deployment {
    metadata {
      migrationActivation "Reader-ready migrations use the production release lock and exact live candidate. The trusted main gate loads with Node built-ins before candidate dependency preparation. Activation clients derive the candidate's production deployment config and a fresh Command attempt before evaluating its stack. A Bun client opens the pool history operator through the existing private Node IPC bridge because Wrangler remote bindings require Node's dispatcher. The bridge preserves the operator report and plan fingerprint inputs. A material plan digest binds serving reader versions, signed singleton adoption, installed app versions and exact database preparations. Encrypted pending intent precedes one activation send; an unknown reply blocks ordinary release until inspected. Read-only inspection never creates or resends an activation. Normal preparation never activates, and later releases retain recognized optional cutover markers."
    }
  }
}
